.SS "void csmp::LinearTriangle3D::IntegralNN (\fBDenseMatrix\fP< DM_MIN > & CE)\fR [virtual]\fP"

.PP
integral over interpolation functions Computes the 'mass' matrix for the element for the case where the factor which is used to multiply the matrix with is constant on the element and can therefore be put in front of the integral\&. 
.br
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
The coordinates of the \fBElement\fP are retrieved in order to calculate its area\&. 
.br

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fICE\fP The mass matrix (nodes x nodes) is returned into the second argument of the method\&. This is a Meschach++ matrix which will be automatically resized if it has not got the correct dimensions\&. 
.br
.RE
.PP
.SH "Implementation"
.PP
The mass matrix = Integral Ni Nj dx dy dz is explained in many FE text books\&. For instance in 'Groundwater Modeling by the Finite \fBElement\fP Method" AGU Monograph 13 by Jonathan Istok\&. The resulting matrix is output in its consistent form\&. 
.br
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
For example, to compute the element 'capacitance' matrix for transient fluid flow\&. 
.PP
